{
  "note": [
    "The syntax sections and the outline call rules (the subprogram-call patterns) of every built-in profile, pinned for M9 by its prelude P9 (plan section 6 M9, P9 item 4; section 7.1, 'The M9 syntax pins').",
    "Read by tests/unit/syntaxPins.test.ts against the resolved built-ins. 'pinned' is the state of the P9 commit. 'deferred' are values P9 decided but could not write without changing an existing golden or snapshot (section 5.2 rule 2): WP9.3 writes exactly these into the profile JSON, with the golden changes they cause, and the test accepts either value until I9 folds them into 'pinned'.",
    "Any other change to a pinned member during M9 is a hand-off note to the integration (I9), which applies it and updates this file. A content work package never edits it.",
    "M10 review (NC-9): the block skip of the Fanuc and Sinumerik profiles gains plainLevel, the level the bare mark is (BDT1 on Fanuc, /0 on Sinumerik): a named pin change.",
    "Integration I9 folded the three deferred values (Fanuc function and print names, Klartext PLANE and TCPM words, the short Sinumerik header) into 'pinned'; 'deferred' is empty. A later value that cannot be written without changing an existing golden goes into 'deferred' again.",
    "Owner answers of 2026-10-08 (plan section 7.16 #172, #175): Klartext gains symbolAddresses ['#'] (the datum-table row of cycle 7), and removeSpaces is 'refuse' on the two Sinumerik profiles and 'keepAroundLongAddresses' on Okuma: named pin changes.",
    "M12.5 WP-RP2 (plan section 7.16 #179, decision 7): the syntax members freeText, colonWords and tapeMarker (Klartext), callTargets, the keywords NOEX, DRAW, CLEAR and the system variables VTL... (Okuma), labelAfter, declareAfter and the keywords SBLOF, SBLON, DISPLOF, DISPLON, NORM, KONT, KONTC, KONTT (Sinumerik, and so Sinumerik milling), plainTextRun (Fanuc, and so the lathe): named pin changes, written by the work package for its gates and to be checked by the integration.",
    "M12.5 integration (plan section 7.16 #185): the Sinumerik header accepts a leading semicolon, so a commented archive header names the program in the map; and the jump-target label is not read when the name is an R parameter (a tokenizer rule, no pinned member): named pin change."
  ],
